    "tpa_score_new": null,
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": null,
    "course_pol_en": "Attendance:\nAttendance is an integral part of the course and is expcted from all students. If a student has a serious illness that results in missing class for more\nthan one week, documentation must be scanned and provided to the instructor via email and/or FCU apps.\n\nPolicy on Missed Talks or failure to submit the report:You must report these circumstances as soon as possible after the\nevent. You may be required to provide documentation as evidences.\nAny reports submitted after the due date will be considered late and may receive a grade of zero, unless there are good reasons.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Academic misconduct refers to practices that a student or a researcher is aware of but deliberately and significantly deviates from the<br />\ngenreallyaccepted academic behavior, such as fabrication, falsification, plagiarism and any act of dishonesty in any forms. Depending on the<br />\nresearch stage,research misconduct can be divided into five types:</div>\n\n<div>1. inappropriate data collection or unrelated information</div>\n\n<div>2. fabrication (falsification) of &nbsp;data related to&nbsp; seminar talks</div>\n\n<div>3. plagiarism</div>\n\n<div>4. inappropriate authorship or designation&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>5. suplicate submission, publication, and applications</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>Penalties for academic misconduct can<br />\nrange from a grade of zero of the assignment(s)/assessment(s) to a penalty as severe as suspension formultiple dishonest acts reported.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
